---
title: React Adapter
description: Understand the thin React lifecycle, SSR, hydration, update, sizing, class, and style behavior around the shared chart host.
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react"},{"type":"text","value":" is a thin lifecycle and SSR adapter around\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts"},{"type":"text","value":". Chart definitions, scale resolution, guide layout, scenes,\nrendering, animation, and interaction remain in the framework-neutral core."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"public-exports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Public exports"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\n\nexport type {\n  ChartCommonProps,\n  ChartProps,\n  ChartDefinition,\n  ChartPoint,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose Canvas or an application-supplied renderer through an explicit\nsubpath:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Chart as CanvasChart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/canvas'\nimport { Chart as RendererChart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/core'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CanvasChart"},{"type":"text","value":" selects the optional built-in renderer. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RendererChart"},{"type":"text","value":" requires\na "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderer"},{"type":"text","value":" prop. The default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" remains SVG-based, so importing the\ndefault adapter does not pull Canvas into its module graph. A definition can\nstill import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" and assign it to selected marks, which makes\nthe default component render an ordered mixed surface."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The base entries render the built-in tooltip without the React tooltip-body\nbridge. Import from the optional tooltip entry when passing\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  Chart,\n  CanvasChart,\n  RendererChart,\n  type ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":" users should move the default component import\nfrom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":". For Canvas\nor an application renderer, replace the aliased "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/canvas"},{"type":"text","value":"\nor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/core"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CanvasChart"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RendererChart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the re-exported definition and point types only when an application API\nneeds an explicit annotation. Ordinary component use is inferred."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"render-lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render lifecycle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter creates one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRuntime"},{"type":"text","value":" per mounted component and asks the\nselected renderer for its initial markup during React render. After commit:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a layout effect mounts the shared DOM host into the existing chart surface"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the same runtime is passed to the host"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a second layout effect forwards the latest complete host options"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"later React commits call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"host.update"},{"type":"text","value":"; a new definition identity rebuilds\nthe scene"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"effect cleanup destroys the host and runtime-owned browser behavior"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The chart surface is memoized after its first render. Scene changes are painted\nby the shared host rather than by rebuilding the surface through React.\nMemoize definitions that capture component values with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMemo"},{"type":"text","value":"; module-scope\ndefinitions need no component memoization."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React batching may omit intermediate application states. Every committed prop\nset forwarded to the host remains declarative and complete."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ssr-and-hydration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR and hydration"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"next-js-app-router","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next.js App Router"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React chart entries include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'use client'"},{"type":"text","value":". This identifies the React Server\nComponent boundary, it does not disable server-rendered SVG."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Put the chart definition, configured scales, renderers, and callbacks inside\nyour application's client component. Pass data from a Server Component, not a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChart()"},{"type":"text","value":" result. Definitions contain functions and scale instances that\ncannot cross that boundary as serializable props."}]},{"type":"code","value":"'use client'\n\nimport { useMemo } from 'react'\nimport { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\n\nexport function TrafficChart({\n  rows,\n}: {\n  rows: { hour: number; visits: number }[]\n}) {\n  const definition = useMemo(\n    () =>\n      defineChart({\n        marks: [lineY(rows, { x: 'hour', y: 'visits' })],\n        scales: { x: { scale: scaleLinear }, y: { scale: scaleLinear } },\n      }),\n    [rows],\n  )\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={definition}\n      ariaLabel=\"Hourly traffic\"\n      initialWidth={720}\n      height={260}\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same boundary applies to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/react/core"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/react/canvas"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/react/tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":",\nand the corresponding "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-charts"},{"type":"text","value":" entries. See Next.js's\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://nextjs.org/docs/app/getting-started/server-and-client-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server and Client Components"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor prop serialization and server rendering."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"default-server-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default server output"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default SVG entry emits:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the outer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-host"},{"type":"text","value":" div"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-surface"},{"type":"text","value":" div"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the complete accessible shared SVG at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client renders the same initial structure, then the layout effect adopts\nand reconciles that SVG. There is no placeholder-only server mode."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want to skip server chart rendering, use the application-owned\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../guides/ssr-and-hydration.md#client-only-react-charts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"client-only chart"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\npattern. It preserves the same placeholder during the first browser render."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Canvas entry emits the same outer structure with a named Canvas root and\nfive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-hidden"},{"type":"text","value":" canvases: one hidden stable base bitmap and four live paint\nlayers. It does not paint pixels on the server. The client adopts those\nelements, paints after mount, and attaches the same focus, keyboard, tooltip,\nand selection host."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A default chart with selected Canvas marks emits one mixed root containing\nordered SVG markup and Canvas shells. SVG marks are visible in the server\nresponse, Canvas pixels appear after mount, and the client adopts every child\nsurface."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use deterministic data, scale domains, definitions, dimensions, and custom\nrenderers on server and client. The adapter generates a sanitized "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"},{"type":"text","value":"\nfrom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"React.useId()"},{"type":"text","value":" when one is not supplied, keeping document resources\nstable through hydration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tabIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" on both server and client. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyboard: false"},{"type":"text","value":" forces\nit to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default SVG renderer emits gradients and clipping on both server and\nclient. Custom serializers must preserve the same resources. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/rendering-and-export.md#svg-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering and export"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"sizing-and-layout","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sizing and layout"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter renders two nested containers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".ts-chart-host\n  .ts-chart-surface\n    svg.ts-chart | div.ts-chart-canvas | div.ts-chart-layers","lang":"text"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The outer host has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"position: relative"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Props"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outer host behavior"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scene behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":", fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width: 100%"},{"type":"text","value":"; fixed height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"container width × fixed height"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed CSS width and height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"same fixed scene dimensions"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed width and CSS ratio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed width divided by ratio"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"positive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":", no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width: 100%"},{"type":"text","value":"; CSS aspect ratio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"measured width divided by ratio"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"neither "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" nor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width: 100%"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height: 320px"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"measured width × 320"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"640"},{"type":"text","value":" and controls the initial/server scene when\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" is absent. A fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" takes precedence over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":".\nNonpositive and nonfinite ratios fall back to the default height."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The DOM host observes responsive dimensions and measures the inherited\ncontainer font. Its exact fallback and relayout behavior is documented in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/dom-host.md#responsive-sizing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DOM host"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"classname-and-style","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React-specific presentation props apply to the outer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-host"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue\"\n  className=\"dashboard-chart\"\n  style={{ minHeight: 240, color: 'var(--foreground)' }}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":" is appended after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ts-chart-host"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"React.CSSProperties"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"custom style fields override the adapter's computed position, width, height,\nand aspect ratio because they are spread last."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not give "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style.width"},{"type":"text","value":" a value that conflicts with a fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" prop. The\nstyle controls the outer CSS box, while the prop continues to lock the scene\nwidth. A custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style.height"},{"type":"text","value":" remains live when both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" are absent. Either sizing prop stays authoritative over CSS\nheight when supplied."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core renderer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":" options apply to a surface when calling it directly.\nThe React adapter's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":" intentionally owns the outer element instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tooltip-body-composition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip body composition"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The components from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":" accept\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":", which mounts React content into the built-in tooltip\nsurface. Its context provides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"points"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultBody"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pinned"},{"type":"text","value":",\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dismiss"},{"type":"text","value":". Composing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultBody"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the core title, rows, formatting,\nand swatches; arbitrary React content can sit beside it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The shared host owns a stable body mount target and releases it when the\ntooltip is hidden, custom rendering is disabled, or the chart is destroyed.\nReact owns the rendered component lifecycle. A custom body is inert while\ntransient, so display-only content can remain visible but controls should\nrender only while "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pinned"},{"type":"text","value":" is true. Adding the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"portal"},{"type":"text","value":" extension to the\ntooltip options promotes the whole surface above clipped ancestors without\nchanging this React API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For pin-only detail, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visibility: 'pinned'"},{"type":"text","value":" in the definition. The shared\nhost then mounts the native surface and React body only after activation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"definition-identity","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition identity"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define a fixed chart outside component render:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For live state, memoize the complete definition against the values it captures.\nDefinition identity is the application update boundary; see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart Definition API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"callback-freshness","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callback freshness"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every committed prop set is forwarded to the host. Focus, grouped focus,\nselection, and render callbacks therefore use the latest committed functions.\nCallback types are inferred from the definition's marks."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"core-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter does not redefine:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"marks or chart specs"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scale selection and data-preparation ownership"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tooltip and focus semantics"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"animation and reconciliation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"custom marks or renderers"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"link","href":"../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scales"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the injected primitive\nboundary and the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/index.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"core reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for those APIs."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"public-exports","text":"Public exports","level":2},{"id":"render-lifecycle","text":"Render lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"ssr-and-hydration","text":"SSR and hydration","level":2},{"id":"next-js-app-router","text":"Next.js App Router","level":3},{"id":"default-server-output","text":"Default server output","level":3},{"id":"sizing-and-layout","text":"Sizing and layout","level":2},{"id":"classname-and-style","text":"className and style","level":2},{"id":"tooltip-body-composition","text":"Tooltip body composition","level":2},{"id":"definition-identity","text":"Definition identity","level":2},{"id":"callback-freshness","text":"Callback freshness","level":2},{"id":"core-boundary","text":"Core boundary","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`@tanstack/charts/react` is a thin lifecycle and SSR adapter around\n`@tanstack/charts`. Chart definitions, scale resolution, guide layout, scenes,\nrendering, animation, and interaction remain in the framework-neutral core.\n\n## Public exports\n\n```ts\nexport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\n\nexport type {\n  ChartCommonProps,\n  ChartProps,\n  ChartDefinition,\n  ChartPoint,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react'\n```\n\nChoose Canvas or an application-supplied renderer through an explicit\nsubpath:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Chart as CanvasChart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/canvas'\nimport { Chart as RendererChart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/core'\n```\n\n`CanvasChart` selects the optional built-in renderer. `RendererChart` requires\na `renderer` prop. The default `Chart` remains SVG-based, so importing the\ndefault adapter does not pull Canvas into its module graph. A definition can\nstill import `canvasChartRenderer` and assign it to selected marks, which makes\nthe default component render an ordered mixed surface.\n\nThe base entries render the built-in tooltip without the React tooltip-body\nbridge. Import from the optional tooltip entry when passing\n`renderTooltipBody`:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  Chart,\n  CanvasChart,\n  RendererChart,\n  type ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip'\n```\n\nExisting `renderTooltipBody` users should move the default component import\nfrom `@tanstack/charts/react` to `@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip`. For Canvas\nor an application renderer, replace the aliased `Chart` import from `/canvas`\nor `/core` with `CanvasChart` or `RendererChart` from `/tooltip`.\n\nUse the re-exported definition and point types only when an application API\nneeds an explicit annotation. Ordinary component use is inferred.\n\n## Render lifecycle\n\nThe adapter creates one `ChartRuntime` per mounted component and asks the\nselected renderer for its initial markup during React render. After commit:\n\n1. a layout effect mounts the shared DOM host into the existing chart surface\n2. the same runtime is passed to the host\n3. a second layout effect forwards the latest complete host options\n4. later React commits call `host.update`; a new definition identity rebuilds\n   the scene\n5. effect cleanup destroys the host and runtime-owned browser behavior\n\nThe chart surface is memoized after its first render. Scene changes are painted\nby the shared host rather than by rebuilding the surface through React.\nMemoize definitions that capture component values with `useMemo`; module-scope\ndefinitions need no component memoization.\n\nReact batching may omit intermediate application states. Every committed prop\nset forwarded to the host remains declarative and complete.\n\n## SSR and hydration\n\n### Next.js App Router\n\nReact chart entries include `'use client'`. This identifies the React Server\nComponent boundary, it does not disable server-rendered SVG.\n\nPut the chart definition, configured scales, renderers, and callbacks inside\nyour application's client component. Pass data from a Server Component, not a\n`defineChart()` result. Definitions contain functions and scale instances that\ncannot cross that boundary as serializable props.\n\n```tsx\n'use client'\n\nimport { useMemo } from 'react'\nimport { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\n\nexport function TrafficChart({\n  rows,\n}: {\n  rows: { hour: number; visits: number }[]\n}) {\n  const definition = useMemo(\n    () =>\n      defineChart({\n        marks: [lineY(rows, { x: 'hour', y: 'visits' })],\n        scales: { x: { scale: scaleLinear }, y: { scale: scaleLinear } },\n      }),\n    [rows],\n  )\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={definition}\n      ariaLabel=\"Hourly traffic\"\n      initialWidth={720}\n      height={260}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe same boundary applies to `/react/core`, `/react/canvas`, `/react/tooltip`,\nand the corresponding `@tanstack/react-charts` entries. See Next.js's\n[Server and Client Components](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/getting-started/server-and-client-components)\nfor prop serialization and server rendering.\n\n### Default server output\n\nThe default SVG entry emits:\n\n- the outer `.ts-chart-host` div\n- a `.ts-chart-surface` div\n- the complete accessible shared SVG at `initialWidth`\n\nThe client renders the same initial structure, then the layout effect adopts\nand reconciles that SVG. There is no placeholder-only server mode.\n\nIf you want to skip server chart rendering, use the application-owned\n[client-only chart](../../guides/ssr-and-hydration.md#client-only-react-charts)\npattern. It preserves the same placeholder during the first browser render.\n\nThe Canvas entry emits the same outer structure with a named Canvas root and\nfive `aria-hidden` canvases: one hidden stable base bitmap and four live paint\nlayers. It does not paint pixels on the server. The client adopts those\nelements, paints after mount, and attaches the same focus, keyboard, tooltip,\nand selection host.\n\nA default chart with selected Canvas marks emits one mixed root containing\nordered SVG markup and Canvas shells. SVG marks are visible in the server\nresponse, Canvas pixels appear after mount, and the client adopts every child\nsurface.\n\nUse deterministic data, scale domains, definitions, dimensions, and custom\nrenderers on server and client. The adapter generates a sanitized `idPrefix`\nfrom `React.useId()` when one is not supplied, keeping document resources\nstable through hydration.\n\n`tabIndex` defaults to `0` on both server and client. `keyboard: false` forces\nit to `-1`.\n\nThe default SVG renderer emits gradients and clipping on both server and\nclient. Custom serializers must preserve the same resources. See\n[Rendering and export](../../reference/rendering-and-export.md#svg-resources).\n\n## Sizing and layout\n\nThe adapter renders two nested containers:\n\n```text\n.ts-chart-host\n  .ts-chart-surface\n    svg.ts-chart | div.ts-chart-canvas | div.ts-chart-layers\n```\n\nThe outer host has `position: relative`.\n\n| Props                               | Outer host behavior             | Scene behavior                  |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| no `width`, fixed `height`          | `width: 100%`; fixed height     | container width × fixed height  |\n| fixed `width` and `height`          | fixed CSS width and height      | same fixed scene dimensions     |\n| fixed `width` and `aspectRatio`     | fixed width and CSS ratio       | fixed width divided by ratio    |\n| positive `aspectRatio`, no `height` | `width: 100%`; CSS aspect ratio | measured width divided by ratio |\n| neither `height` nor `aspectRatio`  | `width: 100%`; `height: 320px`  | measured width × 320            |\n\n`initialWidth` defaults to `640` and controls the initial/server scene when\n`width` is absent. A fixed `height` takes precedence over `aspectRatio`.\nNonpositive and nonfinite ratios fall back to the default height.\n\nThe DOM host observes responsive dimensions and measures the inherited\ncontainer font. Its exact fallback and relayout behavior is documented in\n[DOM host](../../reference/dom-host.md#responsive-sizing).\n\n## `className` and `style`\n\nReact-specific presentation props apply to the outer `.ts-chart-host`:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue\"\n  className=\"dashboard-chart\"\n  style={{ minHeight: 240, color: 'var(--foreground)' }}\n/>\n```\n\n- `className` is appended after `ts-chart-host`.\n- `style` is `React.CSSProperties`.\n- custom style fields override the adapter's computed position, width, height,\n  and aspect ratio because they are spread last.\n\nDo not give `style.width` a value that conflicts with a fixed `width` prop. The\nstyle controls the outer CSS box, while the prop continues to lock the scene\nwidth. A custom `style.height` remains live when both `height` and\n`aspectRatio` are absent. Either sizing prop stays authoritative over CSS\nheight when supplied.\n\nCore renderer `className` options apply to a surface when calling it directly.\nThe React adapter's `className` intentionally owns the outer element instead.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\nThe components from `@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip` accept\n`renderTooltipBody`, which mounts React content into the built-in tooltip\nsurface. Its context provides `points`, `content`, `defaultBody`, `pinned`,\nand `dismiss`. Composing `defaultBody` keeps the core title, rows, formatting,\nand swatches; arbitrary React content can sit beside it.\n\nThe shared host owns a stable body mount target and releases it when the\ntooltip is hidden, custom rendering is disabled, or the chart is destroyed.\nReact owns the rendered component lifecycle. A custom body is inert while\ntransient, so display-only content can remain visible but controls should\nrender only while `pinned` is true. Adding the `portal` extension to the\ntooltip options promotes the whole surface above clipped ancestors without\nchanging this React API.\n\nFor pin-only detail, set `visibility: 'pinned'` in the definition. The shared\nhost then mounts the native surface and React body only after activation.\n\n## Definition identity\n\nDefine a fixed chart outside component render:\n\n```tsx\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nFor live state, memoize the complete definition against the values it captures.\nDefinition identity is the application update boundary; see\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## Callback freshness\n\nEvery committed prop set is forwarded to the host. Focus, grouped focus,\nselection, and render callbacks therefore use the latest committed functions.\nCallback types are inferred from the definition's marks.\n\n## Core boundary\n\nThe adapter does not redefine:\n\n- marks or chart specs\n- scale selection and data-preparation ownership\n- tooltip and focus semantics\n- animation and reconciliation\n- custom marks or renderers\n\nUse [Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md) for the injected primitive\nboundary and the [core reference](../../reference/index.md) for those APIs.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: React Adapter\ndescription: Understand the thin React lifecycle, SSR, hydration, update, sizing, class, and style behavior around the shared chart host.\n---\n\n`@tanstack/charts/react` is a thin lifecycle and SSR adapter around\n`@tanstack/charts`. Chart definitions, scale resolution, guide layout, scenes,\nrendering, animation, and interaction remain in the framework-neutral core.\n\n## Public exports\n\n```ts\nexport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\n\nexport type {\n  ChartCommonProps,\n  ChartProps,\n  ChartDefinition,\n  ChartPoint,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react'\n```\n\nChoose Canvas or an application-supplied renderer through an explicit\nsubpath:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Chart as CanvasChart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/canvas'\nimport { Chart as RendererChart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/core'\n```\n\n`CanvasChart` selects the optional built-in renderer. `RendererChart` requires\na `renderer` prop. The default `Chart` remains SVG-based, so importing the\ndefault adapter does not pull Canvas into its module graph. A definition can\nstill import `canvasChartRenderer` and assign it to selected marks, which makes\nthe default component render an ordered mixed surface.\n\nThe base entries render the built-in tooltip without the React tooltip-body\nbridge. Import from the optional tooltip entry when passing\n`renderTooltipBody`:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  Chart,\n  CanvasChart,\n  RendererChart,\n  type ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip'\n```\n\nExisting `renderTooltipBody` users should move the default component import\nfrom `@tanstack/charts/react` to `@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip`. For Canvas\nor an application renderer, replace the aliased `Chart` import from `/canvas`\nor `/core` with `CanvasChart` or `RendererChart` from `/tooltip`.\n\nUse the re-exported definition and point types only when an application API\nneeds an explicit annotation. Ordinary component use is inferred.\n\n## Render lifecycle\n\nThe adapter creates one `ChartRuntime` per mounted component and asks the\nselected renderer for its initial markup during React render. After commit:\n\n1. a layout effect mounts the shared DOM host into the existing chart surface\n2. the same runtime is passed to the host\n3. a second layout effect forwards the latest complete host options\n4. later React commits call `host.update`; a new definition identity rebuilds\n   the scene\n5. effect cleanup destroys the host and runtime-owned browser behavior\n\nThe chart surface is memoized after its first render. Scene changes are painted\nby the shared host rather than by rebuilding the surface through React.\nMemoize definitions that capture component values with `useMemo`; module-scope\ndefinitions need no component memoization.\n\nReact batching may omit intermediate application states. Every committed prop\nset forwarded to the host remains declarative and complete.\n\n## SSR and hydration\n\n### Next.js App Router\n\nReact chart entries include `'use client'`. This identifies the React Server\nComponent boundary, it does not disable server-rendered SVG.\n\nPut the chart definition, configured scales, renderers, and callbacks inside\nyour application's client component. Pass data from a Server Component, not a\n`defineChart()` result. Definitions contain functions and scale instances that\ncannot cross that boundary as serializable props.\n\n```tsx\n'use client'\n\nimport { useMemo } from 'react'\nimport { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\n\nexport function TrafficChart({\n  rows,\n}: {\n  rows: { hour: number; visits: number }[]\n}) {\n  const definition = useMemo(\n    () =>\n      defineChart({\n        marks: [lineY(rows, { x: 'hour', y: 'visits' })],\n        scales: { x: { scale: scaleLinear }, y: { scale: scaleLinear } },\n      }),\n    [rows],\n  )\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={definition}\n      ariaLabel=\"Hourly traffic\"\n      initialWidth={720}\n      height={260}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe same boundary applies to `/react/core`, `/react/canvas`, `/react/tooltip`,\nand the corresponding `@tanstack/react-charts` entries. See Next.js's\n[Server and Client Components](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/getting-started/server-and-client-components)\nfor prop serialization and server rendering.\n\n### Default server output\n\nThe default SVG entry emits:\n\n- the outer `.ts-chart-host` div\n- a `.ts-chart-surface` div\n- the complete accessible shared SVG at `initialWidth`\n\nThe client renders the same initial structure, then the layout effect adopts\nand reconciles that SVG. There is no placeholder-only server mode.\n\nIf you want to skip server chart rendering, use the application-owned\n[client-only chart](../../guides/ssr-and-hydration.md#client-only-react-charts)\npattern. It preserves the same placeholder during the first browser render.\n\nThe Canvas entry emits the same outer structure with a named Canvas root and\nfive `aria-hidden` canvases: one hidden stable base bitmap and four live paint\nlayers. It does not paint pixels on the server. The client adopts those\nelements, paints after mount, and attaches the same focus, keyboard, tooltip,\nand selection host.\n\nA default chart with selected Canvas marks emits one mixed root containing\nordered SVG markup and Canvas shells. SVG marks are visible in the server\nresponse, Canvas pixels appear after mount, and the client adopts every child\nsurface.\n\nUse deterministic data, scale domains, definitions, dimensions, and custom\nrenderers on server and client. The adapter generates a sanitized `idPrefix`\nfrom `React.useId()` when one is not supplied, keeping document resources\nstable through hydration.\n\n`tabIndex` defaults to `0` on both server and client. `keyboard: false` forces\nit to `-1`.\n\nThe default SVG renderer emits gradients and clipping on both server and\nclient. Custom serializers must preserve the same resources. See\n[Rendering and export](../../reference/rendering-and-export.md#svg-resources).\n\n## Sizing and layout\n\nThe adapter renders two nested containers:\n\n```text\n.ts-chart-host\n  .ts-chart-surface\n    svg.ts-chart | div.ts-chart-canvas | div.ts-chart-layers\n```\n\nThe outer host has `position: relative`.\n\n| Props                               | Outer host behavior             | Scene behavior                  |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| no `width`, fixed `height`          | `width: 100%`; fixed height     | container width × fixed height  |\n| fixed `width` and `height`          | fixed CSS width and height      | same fixed scene dimensions     |\n| fixed `width` and `aspectRatio`     | fixed width and CSS ratio       | fixed width divided by ratio    |\n| positive `aspectRatio`, no `height` | `width: 100%`; CSS aspect ratio | measured width divided by ratio |\n| neither `height` nor `aspectRatio`  | `width: 100%`; `height: 320px`  | measured width × 320            |\n\n`initialWidth` defaults to `640` and controls the initial/server scene when\n`width` is absent. A fixed `height` takes precedence over `aspectRatio`.\nNonpositive and nonfinite ratios fall back to the default height.\n\nThe DOM host observes responsive dimensions and measures the inherited\ncontainer font. Its exact fallback and relayout behavior is documented in\n[DOM host](../../reference/dom-host.md#responsive-sizing).\n\n## `className` and `style`\n\nReact-specific presentation props apply to the outer `.ts-chart-host`:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue\"\n  className=\"dashboard-chart\"\n  style={{ minHeight: 240, color: 'var(--foreground)' }}\n/>\n```\n\n- `className` is appended after `ts-chart-host`.\n- `style` is `React.CSSProperties`.\n- custom style fields override the adapter's computed position, width, height,\n  and aspect ratio because they are spread last.\n\nDo not give `style.width` a value that conflicts with a fixed `width` prop. The\nstyle controls the outer CSS box, while the prop continues to lock the scene\nwidth. A custom `style.height` remains live when both `height` and\n`aspectRatio` are absent. Either sizing prop stays authoritative over CSS\nheight when supplied.\n\nCore renderer `className` options apply to a surface when calling it directly.\nThe React adapter's `className` intentionally owns the outer element instead.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\nThe components from `@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip` accept\n`renderTooltipBody`, which mounts React content into the built-in tooltip\nsurface. Its context provides `points`, `content`, `defaultBody`, `pinned`,\nand `dismiss`. Composing `defaultBody` keeps the core title, rows, formatting,\nand swatches; arbitrary React content can sit beside it.\n\nThe shared host owns a stable body mount target and releases it when the\ntooltip is hidden, custom rendering is disabled, or the chart is destroyed.\nReact owns the rendered component lifecycle. A custom body is inert while\ntransient, so display-only content can remain visible but controls should\nrender only while `pinned` is true. Adding the `portal` extension to the\ntooltip options promotes the whole surface above clipped ancestors without\nchanging this React API.\n\nFor pin-only detail, set `visibility: 'pinned'` in the definition. The shared\nhost then mounts the native surface and React body only after activation.\n\n## Definition identity\n\nDefine a fixed chart outside component render:\n\n```tsx\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nFor live state, memoize the complete definition against the values it captures.\nDefinition identity is the application update boundary; see\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## Callback freshness\n\nEvery committed prop set is forwarded to the host. Focus, grouped focus,\nselection, and render callbacks therefore use the latest committed functions.\nCallback types are inferred from the definition's marks.\n\n## Core boundary\n\nThe adapter does not redefine:\n\n- marks or chart specs\n- scale selection and data-preparation ownership\n- tooltip and focus semantics\n- animation and reconciliation\n- custom marks or renderers\n\nUse [Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md) for the injected primitive\nboundary and the [core reference](../../reference/index.md) for those APIs.\n"}
